WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.305 --> 00:00:06.072
&gt;&gt; NEIL: ALL RIGHT, ANOTHER BIG

00:00:06.073 --> 00:00:07.263
&gt;&gt; NEIL: ALL RIGHT, ANOTHER BIG

00:00:07.265 --> 00:00:09.215
COMPANY FROM SILICON VALLEY IS

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.218
SAYING GOOD-BYE TO SILICON

00:00:10.252 --> 00:00:10.938
VALLEY.

00:00:10.939 --> 00:00:12.571
NOT ENTIRELY, BUT HEWLETT

00:00:12.606 --> 00:00:14.323
PACKARD ENTERPRISES IS GOING TO

00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:17.122
MOVE A LOT OF THE OPERATIONS TO

00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:18.273
HOUSTON, TEXAS.

00:00:18.274 --> 00:00:20.227
THE MAYOR OF SAN JOSE HAS BEEN

00:00:20.262 --> 00:00:21.797
DOING HIS BEST TO STOP THIS SORT

00:00:21.799 --> 00:00:22.627
OF THING.

00:00:22.661 --> 00:00:23.663
IT’S HAPPENING YET AGAIN.

00:00:23.665 --> 00:00:26.120
MAYOR, GOOD TO HAVE YOU.

00:00:26.121 --> 00:00:29.233
WHAT DO YOU MAKE OF THIS?

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.160
NOW, IT LOOKS LIKE READING

00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:32.970
HEWLETT PACKARD’S COMMENTS ON

00:00:32.971 --> 00:00:35.053
THIS, IT’S NOT ABANDONING YOUR

00:00:35.054 --> 00:00:36.908
AREA, BUT IT’S CUTTING DOWN ITS

00:00:36.942 --> 00:00:38.996
PRESENCE IN YOUR AREA.

00:00:38.997 --> 00:00:40.660
DOES IT ALARM YOU?

00:00:40.694 --> 00:00:42.849
&gt;&gt; WELL, CERTAINLY IT’S A WAKEUP

00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:44.507
CALL FOR ALL OF US, NEIL.

00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:47.795
AND THE GOOD NEWS IS HERE IN THE

00:00:47.796 --> 00:00:50.537
CITY OF SAN JOSE, WE’RE ADDING

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:52.367
HUNDREDS OF EMPLOYEES BECAUSE

00:00:52.368 --> 00:00:53.711
THEY’RE CONSOLIDATING OPERATIONS

00:00:53.712 --> 00:00:55.229
HERE FROM SILICON VALLEY AND MY

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:55.716
CITY.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:56.878
WE’RE SEEING HEADQUARTERS MOVE

00:00:56.913 --> 00:00:57.423
BE.

00:00:57.425 --> 00:00:59.115
THIS IS A STORY WE’VE SEEN

00:00:59.150 --> 00:00:59.685
BEFORE.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.792
THAT CERTAINLY FOR THE KIND OF

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:05.223
TALENT THAT YOU REALLY NEED TO

00:01:05.258 --> 00:01:07.643
FIND IN SILICON VALLEY, THE

00:01:07.644 --> 00:01:09.506
HIGHLY SPECIALIZED AROUND

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.939
ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE OR

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.158
ENGINEERING OR SOFTWARE, YOU’LL

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.947
FIND IT IN SILICON VALLEY AND

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:15.050
THE FOLKS THAT WANT TO LOCATE

00:01:15.051 --> 00:01:15.632
HERE.

00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:18.292
BUT IF YOU’RE LOOKING TO EXPAND

00:01:18.294 --> 00:01:19.932
OPERATIONS FOR ACCOUNTANTS OR

00:01:19.967 --> 00:01:20.774
LAWYERS OR ADMINISTRATIVE

00:01:20.775 --> 00:01:22.980
ASSISTANTS, YOU CAN DO THAT FOR

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.362
A LOT OF PLACES FOR A LOT LESS.

00:01:25.363 --> 00:01:26.972
AND, WE HAVE TO DO MORE TO MAKE

00:01:27.006 --> 00:01:29.296
THIS REGION AND THIS STATE MORE

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:29.777
AFFORDABLE.

00:01:29.811 --> 00:01:32.519
&gt;&gt; NEIL: YOU’VE BEEN KIND OF --

00:01:32.553 --> 00:01:34.589
YOU WERE RE-ELECTED IN 2018 WITH

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.617
MORE THAN 70, WHAT, 5% OF THE

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:38.341
VOTE AT THE TIME.

00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:41.746
AND LARGELY BY TAKING ON, YOU

00:01:41.747 --> 00:01:43.307
KNOW, UNIONS AND PENSION-FUNDED

00:01:43.342 --> 00:01:45.174
ORGANIZATIONS WHERE YOU JUST

00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:47.308
WANTED TO EASE BACK ON THOSE

00:01:47.309 --> 00:01:48.509
OBLIGATIONS BECAUSE THEY’RE A

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.629
GOOD REASON WHY SAN JOSE AND

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.686
OTHER AREAS ACROSS THE COUNTRY

00:01:52.687 --> 00:01:54.392
WITH SIMILAR ISSUES ARE SO

00:01:54.393 --> 00:01:55.886
PRICEY AND ARE BEING PRICED OUT

00:01:55.887 --> 00:01:57.137
AND HAVING COMPANIES MOVE.

00:01:57.138 --> 00:01:58.484
BUT THAT APPARENTLY IS NOT

00:01:58.486 --> 00:01:58.733
ENOUGH.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:01.274
SO, WHAT DOES THE STATE HAVE TO

00:02:01.308 --> 00:02:01.745
DO?

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.478
&gt;&gt; WELL, THE BIGGEST CHALLENGE,

00:02:03.513 --> 00:02:06.209
I THINK WE ALL HAVE IS WITH

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:06.958
HOUSING COSTS.

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:08.393
IT’S HARD TO LIVE HERE.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.030
COMPANIES HAVE TO PAY A LOT JUST

00:02:10.031 --> 00:02:10.981
TO KEEP PEOPLE HERE.

00:02:10.982 --> 00:02:12.543
THERE’S A LOT MORE WE NEED TO DO

00:02:12.544 --> 00:02:13.392
TO RAMP UP PRODUCTION.

00:02:13.393 --> 00:02:15.374
WE CAN CERTAINLY GET SOME OF THE

00:02:15.408 --> 00:02:17.019
RED TAPE OUT OF THE WAY.

00:02:17.054 --> 00:02:18.978
AND I APPRECIATE THE RECENT

00:02:18.979 --> 00:02:21.841
EFFORTS OF THE GOVERNOR, FOR

00:02:21.842 --> 00:02:24.546
EXAMPLE, TO BE ABLE TO -- FOR

00:02:24.548 --> 00:02:26.481
EXAMPLE, WAGE ON THE AFFORDABLE

00:02:26.482 --> 00:02:28.839
HOUSING WE NEED FOR HOMELESS

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.456
RESIDENTS THAT ENABLED US TO

00:02:30.491 --> 00:02:31.434
BUILD THREE SEPARATE

00:02:31.469 --> 00:02:32.648
DEVELOPMENTS IN FOUR MONTHS

00:02:32.682 --> 00:02:33.736
RATHER THAN FOUR YEARS.

00:02:33.771 --> 00:02:34.939
THOSE ARE THE THINGS WE NEED TO

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:35.218
DO.

00:02:35.253 --> 00:02:36.393
MOSTLY JUST GETTING OUT OF THE

00:02:36.427 --> 00:02:37.008
WAY.

00:02:37.042 --> 00:02:40.317
WE NEED TO BE MORE INNOVATIVE IN

00:02:40.318 --> 00:02:43.140
HOW WE’RE BUILDING HOUSES.

00:02:43.174 --> 00:02:45.130
WE’RE USING DIFFERENT

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.001
TECHNOLOGIES, PREFAB AND MODULAR

00:02:47.002 --> 00:02:47.546
HOUSING.

00:02:47.547 --> 00:02:49.642
THAT ALLOWS THE LOCAL

00:02:49.676 --> 00:02:51.529
BUREAUCRACIES TO BE NIMBLE, TO

00:02:51.531 --> 00:02:53.308
PERMIT THOSE THINGS AND STILL

00:02:53.342 --> 00:02:54.450
ALLOW THE INNOVATION.

00:02:54.451 --> 00:02:56.386
HOUSING IS AT THE CORE OF IT.

00:02:56.388 --> 00:02:57.915
IT’S A LOT GOING ON.

00:02:57.917 --> 00:02:59.117
TAXES, REGULATION, A LOT OF

00:02:59.151 --> 00:03:01.035
ISSUES WHERE I THINK WE NEED TO

00:03:01.036 --> 00:03:02.644
BE COGNIZANT IN CALIFORNIA.

00:03:02.679 --> 00:03:04.483
WE’VE BEEN TAKING IT FOR GRANTED

00:03:04.485 --> 00:03:07.713
FOR TOO LONG THAT TECH EMPLOYERS

00:03:07.714 --> 00:03:09.421
WANT TO BE HERE.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.444
THAT WON’T HAPPEN FOREVER.

00:03:11.478 --> 00:03:14.244
&gt;&gt; NEIL: DID YOU OFFER AN

00:03:14.245 --> 00:03:17.259
ALTERNATIVE DEAL TO STOP HEWLETT

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.154
PACKARD FROM MAKING THIS MOVE?

00:03:19.155 --> 00:03:21.309
WE’RE BUILDING THIS BIG FACILITY

00:03:21.344 --> 00:03:22.974
IN HOUSTON, WE’RE GOING THERE.

00:03:23.008 --> 00:03:24.957
&gt;&gt; I’VE BEEN CLEAR THAT WE DON’T

00:03:24.991 --> 00:03:26.229
WANT TO OFFER COMPANIES DEALS OF

00:03:26.264 --> 00:03:27.736
ANY KIND.

00:03:27.737 --> 00:03:30.576
WHEN AMAZON WAS ANNOUNCING THE

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:33.145
CONTACTS AT THE MIDDLE OF THE

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.066
HEADQUARTERS, I WROTE AN OP-ED

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.477
SAYING, WE’RE NOT GOING TO GIVE

00:03:36.512 --> 00:03:37.237
YOU MONEY.

00:03:37.271 --> 00:03:39.313
I DON’T BELIEVE GIVING TAXPAYER

00:03:39.314 --> 00:03:40.499
NOUN COMPANIES.

00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:42.539
HP NEVER ASKED FOR IT.

00:03:42.573 --> 00:03:43.708
THEY’VE BEEN ABOVE BOARD WITH

00:03:43.743 --> 00:03:43.971
US.

00:03:44.006 --> 00:03:45.303
I UNDERSTOOD WHY THEY WOULD BE

00:03:45.304 --> 00:03:46.099
GOING TO HOUSTON.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.831
THEY HAVE A LOT OF OPERATIONS

00:03:47.832 --> 00:03:48.936
ALREADY THERE AND A LOT OF

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:49.579
EMPLOYEES.

00:03:49.614 --> 00:03:51.266
BUT, FOR THOSE HEADQUARTERS

00:03:51.268 --> 00:03:52.726
OPERATIONS, YOU DON’T NEED THE

00:03:52.727 --> 00:03:54.645
TECHNICAL -- THEY CAN KEEP ALL

00:03:54.646 --> 00:03:57.014
OF THAT HERE IN SILICON VALLEY

00:03:57.015 --> 00:03:58.578
AND HIRE ELSEWHERE.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:00.817
&gt;&gt; NEIL: YOU KNOW IT’S MORE THAN

00:04:00.851 --> 00:04:02.044
JUST TAXES AND THE COST OF

00:04:02.046 --> 00:04:02.470
LIVING.

00:04:02.504 --> 00:04:04.359
I KNOW YOU ARE EVE APOLOGIZED

00:04:04.361 --> 00:04:06.137
FOR THIS INCIDENT WHERE YOU

00:04:06.139 --> 00:04:07.155
JOINED YOUR FAMILY FOR

00:04:07.189 --> 00:04:07.571
THANKSGIVING.

00:04:07.572 --> 00:04:09.235
IT WAS A LARGE GATHERING, LARGER

00:04:09.236 --> 00:04:10.381
THAN YOU SUSPECTED.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.926
BUT IT CAME AT A TIME WHEN A

00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:15.136
NUMBER OF OTHER TOP POLITICIANS,

00:04:15.138 --> 00:04:18.373
MOSTLY DEMOCRATS HATE TO SAY

00:04:18.408 --> 00:04:21.106
THAT TO YOU, DID ONE THING AND

00:04:21.141 --> 00:04:21.709
PRACTICED ANOTHER.

00:04:21.744 --> 00:04:24.548
DO YOU THINK THAT PEOPLE LOOK AT

00:04:24.549 --> 00:04:26.140
THAT, MAYOR, AND SAY, THE GUY IS

00:04:26.142 --> 00:04:27.728
A HYPOCRITE?

00:04:27.763 --> 00:04:30.850
&gt;&gt; SURE, I -- I RECOGNIZE FOLKS

00:04:30.851 --> 00:04:32.503
THAT COME TO THOSE KINDS OF

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:32.871
CONCLUSIONINGS.

00:04:32.906 --> 00:04:35.762
I MADE A MISTAKE AND I OWNED IT.

00:04:35.796 --> 00:04:38.251
I SHOULD HAVE BEEN MORE ASTUTE

00:04:38.286 --> 00:04:39.984
ABOUT THE SPECIFIC REGULATIONS.

00:04:39.985 --> 00:04:41.985
I KNEW THERE WERE ADVISORIES AND

00:04:41.986 --> 00:04:43.500
I SHOULD HAVE BEEN MORE ASTUTE

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:44.229
TO IT.

00:04:44.264 --> 00:04:46.683
AND, YOU KNOW, I -- AS I LEARNED

00:04:46.717 --> 00:04:49.160
IN THE MEDIA REPORTED THAT I WAS

00:04:49.162 --> 00:04:50.252
AT HOME, WE IMMEDIATELY

00:04:50.286 --> 00:04:50.691
DISCLOSED.

00:04:50.725 --> 00:04:53.428
NO, I WAS AT MY PARENTS’ HOUSE

00:04:53.463 --> 00:04:55.266
AND THAT’S HOW ALL OF THIS CAME

00:04:55.268 --> 00:04:55.622
OUT.

00:04:55.656 --> 00:04:58.960
SO, I -- GOING AND CERTAINLY --

00:04:58.961 --> 00:05:02.131
WILL DO BETTER.

00:05:02.132 --> 00:05:04.760
&gt;&gt; NEIL: WHEN YOU ADDED

00:05:04.762 --> 00:05:06.776
RELATIVES’ HOUSE, THERE’S A BIG

00:05:06.811 --> 00:05:09.205
CROWD HERE AND I’M THE MAYOR OF

00:05:09.239 --> 00:05:11.259
SAN JOSE AND I’VE BEEN TELLING

00:05:11.293 --> 00:05:12.379
MY CONSTITUENTS, KEEP IT SMALL,

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.715
KEEP IT LIMITED.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.451
DID YOU THINK?

00:05:15.485 --> 00:05:16.498
DID YOU --

00:05:16.499 --> 00:05:18.783
&gt;&gt; I CAN’T CLAIM TO HAVE BEEN

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.489
SO -- THE REALITY IS, I HAVE A

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:23.392
BIG FAMILY, I’M ONE OF FIVE

00:05:23.393 --> 00:05:24.794
KIDS, SO TYPICALLY THANKSGIVING

00:05:24.795 --> 00:05:25.964
FOR US IS 25.

00:05:25.965 --> 00:05:27.453
WE ACTUALLY HAD EIGHT ADULTS

00:05:27.454 --> 00:05:28.731
DINING AT THE SAME TIME.

00:05:28.733 --> 00:05:30.311
AND THE PROBLEM WAS UNDER THE

00:05:30.312 --> 00:05:31.930
STATE RULES, YOU CAN ONLY HAVE

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:32.887
THREE HOUSE HOLDS.

00:05:32.888 --> 00:05:34.522
AND SO WE HAD TOO MANY HOUSE

00:05:34.557 --> 00:05:36.744
HOLDS THERE EVEN THOUGH ALL OF

00:05:36.746 --> 00:05:38.554
US, MANY OF US HAD BEEN DINING

00:05:38.555 --> 00:05:40.288
TOGETHER EVERY WEEK.

00:05:40.289 --> 00:05:42.437
THE RULES HAVE CHANGED,

00:05:42.471 --> 00:05:44.978
OBVIOUSLY, WE’VE GONE IN TO

00:05:45.012 --> 00:05:47.364
DEEPER INTO THE -- THE

00:05:47.398 --> 00:05:48.614
CHALLENGING PERIOD OF HIGH

00:05:48.615 --> 00:05:49.309
INFECTION SPREAD.

00:05:49.311 --> 00:05:51.930
AND I SHOULD HAVE KNOWN BETTER.

00:05:51.931 --> 00:05:54.573
I SHOULD HAVE DONE BETTER.

00:05:54.574 --> 00:05:56.540
&gt;&gt; NEIL: UNLIKE A LOT OF

00:05:56.542 --> 00:05:58.318
POLITICIANS THAT DID THE SAME

00:05:58.319 --> 00:06:00.304
THING, YOU GOT AHEAD OF IT AND

00:06:00.306 --> 00:06:01.379
APOLOGIZED FOR IT.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.335
SO, IF MORE DID, MAYBE IT WOULD

00:06:03.336 --> 00:06:04.067
BE EASIER TO MOVE ON.

